Hello again,

I've just uploaded a (somewhat minor) update to my mod.

You can download windows binaries from here: 
https://github.com/karadoc/Nethack/downloads
and source code here: https://github.com/karadoc/Nethack/

Here's a short list of a few interesting changes since the previous version:

+ Implemented new silver short sword artifact: Insanity's Edge.
+ Shop keepers will now pick up any gold that they happen to step onto.
+ 'Hub' style maps are now guaranteed to have at least one random item, 
and one fairly strong random monster in the center room.
+ Corrected a bug which caused crosswalls to be removed in some versions 
of mine-town.
+ Players can now choose between metric and imperial units for the 
weights in the inventory screen.

--

For those who haven't tried this mod (which I imagine is pretty much 
everyone), here's a brief description:
+ There are some new types of random maps, and some new versions of the 
fixed maps to make things a bit more varied and interesting. (eg. new 
"big rooms", a couple of new sokoban levels, and some new (but uncommon) 
layout types for 'standard' dungeons of doom levels.
+ There are lots of balance changes. The early game might be slightly 
easier than before (but not much); and in some cases the late-game will 
be harder - because having well enchanted armour + all resistances is no 
longer enough to make your character effectively invincible.
+ Some weapons and skills have been adjusted to increase the number of 
viable options. For example, scimitars and sabers now share skill point 
slots - so that leveling up your scimitar skill level and your saber 
level will only cost you one set of skill points rather than two sets; 
this makes scimitars more viable. (There are several other such 
pairings.); another example, thrown spears will now do significantly 
more damage for characters who have trained their spear skills - this is 
meant to be analogous to the multi-throw ability gained for daggers and 
other throwing weapons.
+ There are a couple of new items to fill niches that I through needed 
filling. The new items have some interesting new effects...

That's about all.

To anyone who is looking for components to copy from this mod into their 
own nethack stuff - I highly recommend the new sokoban levels; one of 
them in particular is... quite unique. Also, I think the helm of 
anti-magic is a pretty interesting item.

Let me know if you have any problems or feedback or questions or whatever.

(originally I was using sourceforge. I've updated the binaries on 
sourceforge as well, but in general I prefer to us github these days.)


